=== Climate ===
Ishijima Prefecture has a tropical monsoon climate (Köppen climate classification ''Am''), characterized by hot, humid conditions year-round with a distinct wet season driven by the Shendan monsoon. The eastern coast, facing the open Shendan Ocean, receives significantly heavier rainfall than the western Ishijima corridor—approximately 3,200 mm annually compared to Aizawa's 1,744 mm. The monsoon season from May through October brings torrential rainfall and occasional typhoon landfalls, while the November–April dry season is warm and relatively stable.

The volcanic topography creates significant microclimatic variation. The coastal plain is uniformly hot and humid, while the upland communities in the Asuka foothills experience cooler temperatures and frequent fog. The volcanic heat from Mount Ishijima creates localized warm zones that support tropical agriculture at altitudes where it would otherwise be impossible.

